#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Now, in the case of Prophet Muhammadﷺ, he came with that Message We see what are the possibilities, looking at his life, studying his life, that what was he? Now, we already believe in a Creator in this case We're not discussing the belief in a Creator There is a Creator Now, after the belief in a Creator, and there is a Creator, we have the Prophet Muhammadﷺ Now, the question is, if he's claiming to come from that Creator, how did he behave? Now, he could have not said the Truth What he was saying was not saying the Truth If he was not saying the Truth, then there has to be a reason Now, these reasons can be what?", "Financial gain! Why do people lie, usually? Being scared of something, for instance Financial gain Whatever it is, these are reasons why people lie Financial gain or scared or afraid of something Power in the community, to make a change.. These are the reasons why people will say something which isn't true Now, the Prophet Muhammadﷺ, he was promised and he was offered money They came to the Prophet Muhammadﷺ They told him, you stop this mission that you're doing Stop this Message that you're giving And if you want women, we'll give you women If you want to be a leader, we'll make you a leader over us If you want women, we'll give you our own women, as they're saying, and we're making you a leader over us.", "The money, we'll give you money You just name it, and we'll give it to you So, if he was not saying the Truth due to getting financial gain, the first thing he's going to do is Yeah OK! give me, and I'm going to stop I'm going to become the leader I'm going to have money I'm going to have all the women that I want But the Prophet Muhammadﷺ he said, do you see the sun? –in the authentic narration– Because there's many people who quote a different narration This is the most authentic wording, is bring me a piece of that sun If you're able to bring me a piece of that sun, then we talk!", "Meaning, I'm commanded to do this by God This is not something that I'm doing for my own purposes And you see that reflected even more when the Prophetﷺ was in the Medina period Prophet Muhammadﷺ died and his shield was what? Who knows? His shield? Was مرهون, he did رَهن (mortgage) of his shield, with a Jewish person The shield, he was given it to a Jewish person to use it, rent it, and then give him money Now the question is, someone come and ask, Prophet Muhammadﷺ at that time, he was the leader of the Muslims and he had the money, Could have said to Abu Bakr, 'Umar..", "You know, Abu Bakr asSiddiq was rich! 'Uthman, may Allah honour him, was rich! Give me money, give me money, give me money.. Prophet Muhammadﷺ, the scholars explained the reason he did that Is because of his shyness from asking people for money He's not using this, the fact that he's a Messenger of God as a means to get money from people He didn't do that Which is why he rented, he went to someone who's not a Muslim, because if he goes to a Muslim, \"Oh Prophet of Allah, take all what you want\", you know! \"Everything you just ask for it, I'll give it to you\" And he will refuse to take anything from the Prophetﷺ because he is the Messenger of Allah So he went to someone who's not a Muslim, who doesn't believe in his Messengerhood, because he will deal with him justly in that way, and he's not going to try to give him everything", "Which is why; that is what happens When you look at the life of the Prophetﷺ, it's not just before the Message, but also after that It's not only before, but also after So after the Prophet Muhammadﷺ was already established and having all of this power, etc. He also was not seeking financial gain, was not seeking money, was not seeking women, even though he could have gotten whatever he wanted So we know from that, we see from that, that this could not have been the case",))
