ation that you find in Mustadrak al-Hakim which provides additional details. So he says uh that Quraysh said to him, \"You want to Muhammad?\" As in you want to go to Muhammad. And they responded, \"No, we don't. Uh we just want to go to Medina.\" So they said uh so they basically took oaths from Hudhayfah and from his father that they would go to Medina and they would not support the Prophet, peace be upon him, in his battle.", "Okay? I want to give you guys a bit of background here about this. Why this is so cool. This is why this is so interesting. Hudhayfah bin al-Yaman al-Absi. He's from Abs. All right? Those of you that taken had taken the pre-Islam course know why this is so significant. For those that aren't aware, Banu Abs is the fiercest, in my opinion, most dangerous uh Bedouin tribe. Okay? They're all about going to war. They're all about going to war with everyone, you know? They're they're actually going to war with everyone. Um and if you want to learn more about Banu Abs, the easily the most entertaining um uh series of battles in in pre-Islamic history, then you know where to go, the pre-Islam course.", "In any case, he is not among Abs. He's living in Medina. What's going on there? And when I when when that just like clicked in my mind, why isn't Hudhayfah and his father um with their tribe? And I I noticed I was like, hey, wait a second. I don't know too many um companions from the tribe of Abs. What is going on? So, I looked into his biography and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman actually his father uh basically killed someone from his own tribe and then escaped to Medina. All right, Yathrib at the time. And uh Medina is actually south of where Abs lived.", "So, he left his tribe and sought the protection of the people of Medina. Sought the protection specifically of the clan of Banu Abd al-Ashhal which was led by Sa'd ibn Mu'adh. All right? And uh he basically married into them. And not only that, because of his new-found allegiance to them, they started 